PR #4 — Constants, typed routes and content module
Branch: feat/constants-and-routes      Depends on: #3                Status: DONE
───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
DESCRIPTION
  The other half of "no hardcoded values": strings, routes and numbers.

IMPLEMENTS
  [x] site.constants.ts — identity and metadata only; copy moved to content/
  [x] country.constants.ts + document-type.constants.ts — the addressable set,
      declared here because routes exist before the registry (PR #8) does
  [x] routes.constants.ts — typed builders over those unions
  [x] measurement.constants.ts — DPI defaults, mm/inch factors, tolerances
  [x] analysis.constants.ts — every detection threshold, named and commented
  [x] limits.constants.ts — max upload bytes, max pixels, worker timeouts
  [x] content/ — all user-facing copy, keyed, locale-ready
  [x] format-measurement.utils.ts — Intl-based, never concatenates units
  [x] Legal copy lives in content.legal, referenced once

EDGE CASES
  [x] Route builders reject unknown country/document at compile time — they
      take the CountrySlug and DocumentType unions, not strings
  [x] Trailing-slash policy encoded in absoluteUrl; home returns the bare origin
      so it agrees with trailingSlash:false rather than producing two URLs
  [x] Missing copy keys fail the build — ContentTree is declared as an interface
      rather than inferred, so a locale that omits a key fails tsc
  [x] Unit-in-name convention enforced by a test that reflects over the exported
      constants; dimensionless factors declare themselves _RADIX/_SCALE/_FACTOR
  [x] Locale-aware formatting via Intl.NumberFormat — asserted against de-DE,
      which uses a comma decimal separator
  [x] Every error message must name an action, not just a fault — asserted

SEO
  [ ] Canonical URL builder lives here; every page uses it, none hand-rolls one

TESTS
  Unit: exhaustive route-builder cases including invalid input.

