PR #13 — Person segmentation and crown detection
Branch: feat/segmentation-crown        Depends on: #12               Status: TODO
───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
DESCRIPTION
  THE RISKIEST PR IN THE PROJECT. Landmarks stop at the hairline, so crown-to-
  chin — the most common rejection reason — depends entirely on this working.
  Build the hard-case test set BEFORE the implementation.

IMPLEMENTS
  [ ] Segmentation model behind the detector interface
  [ ] Mask cleanup: morphological close, largest-connected-component, hole fill
  [ ] Crown estimation from the cleaned mask
  [ ] Per-result confidence, surfaced when low

EDGE CASES
  [ ] Dark hair against a dark background — the classic failure
  [ ] Bald and shaved heads (crown is skin, not hair)
  [ ] Hats, turbans, hijabs, kippahs — crown of covering vs crown of head
  [ ] Voluminous or curly hair: the spec means the skull, not the hair halo
  [ ] Hair leaving the top of the frame entirely
  [ ] Hair blending into clothing of a similar colour
  [ ] Mask noise, speckle and holes
  [ ] Earrings, glasses arms and jewellery attaching to the mask
  [ ] Someone else's head partly in frame
  [ ] Low-contrast or underexposed source

SEO  n/a

TESTS
  A curated set of ~30 real photos spanning every case above, each with a
  hand-measured ground-truth crown Y. Assert error within tolerance. This
  fixture set is a project asset — document how to extend it.

