  [ ] Source resolution too low to crop at the spec's DPI
  [ ] Extreme source aspect ratios
  [ ] Head correctly sized but positioned so no valid crop exists
  [ ] Rounding must be consistent with PR #9's policy

SEO  n/a

TESTS
  Unit across synthetic geometries plus every fixture from PR #13.

───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
PR #15 — Image quality analysis
Branch: feat/quality-analysis          Depends on: #14               Status: TODO
───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
DESCRIPTION
  Background, shadow, sharpness, exposure and resolution checks over the
  segmentation mask.

IMPLEMENTS
  [ ] Background uniformity: luminance and chroma standard deviation
  [ ] Background colour against the spec's accepted range
  [ ] Shadow detection via background luminance gradient
  [ ] Sharpness via Laplacian variance over the face region
  [ ] Exposure: histogram clipping percentage and mean face luminance
  [ ] Resolution sufficiency against the spec

EDGE CASES
  [ ] Patterned, textured or gradient studio backgrounds
  [ ] White clothing against a white background — segmentation bleed
  [ ] Subject's hair the same tone as the background
  [ ] Deliberate vignetting from a phone camera
  [ ] Motion blur vs shallow depth of field — both blur, only one is the fault
  [ ] Bright but valid exposure vs genuinely clipped highlights
  [ ] Upscaled low-resolution images that "meet" pixel counts but are soft
  [ ] Very small background area when the crop is tight
  [ ] Skin tone must never influence the exposure verdict — test across a
      diverse fixture set, this is a fairness requirement not a nice-to-have

SEO  n/a

TESTS
  Unit against a labelled fixture set, explicitly including diverse skin tones,
  lighting conditions and background types.

───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
PR #16 — Rule engine and compliance report model
Branch: feat/rule-engine               Depends on: #15               Status: TODO
───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
DESCRIPTION
  Measurements plus spec, in. A typed, ordered, human-readable verdict out —
  where every failure carries a physical action the user can take.

IMPLEMENTS
  [ ] Rule definitions with id, severity, confidence and evaluator
  [ ] Verdicts: pass / fail / warning / manual-check / undetectable
  [ ] Fix instructions computed from the delta ("move ~30cm closer")
  [ ] Overall verdict aggregation and rule ordering by importance
  [ ] Manual checklist for glasses, head covering and recency

EDGE CASES
  [ ] Detection failed entirely — must not report "pass" by omission
  [ ] Low-confidence results must degrade to manual-check, never to pass
  [ ] Contradictory rules resolved deterministically
  [ ] Fix instructions must stay correct when two rules interact (moving closer
      fixes head height but may break the eye line)
  [ ] Never emit "guaranteed to pass" anywhere in the model or copy
  [ ] All messages come from the content module — i18n-ready, no literals

SEO  n/a

TESTS
  Unit: every rule, every verdict state, aggregation, message resolution.


