PR #18 — Crop and encode pipeline (mozjpeg byte budget)
Branch: feat/crop-encode               Depends on: #17               Status: TODO
───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
IMPLEMENTS
  [ ] Exact-millimetre crop at the spec's DPI from the full-resolution original
  [ ] mozjpeg encode with binary-search quality to fit the byte ceiling
  [ ] Write correct JFIF density (DPI) metadata into the output
  [ ] sRGB conversion; strip all EXIF including GPS
EDGE CASES
  [ ] Byte ceiling unreachable even at minimum quality => explain, don't fail
  [ ] Source smaller than the required output — never upscale silently
  [ ] Binary search must terminate; cap iterations
  [ ] DPI metadata is a common rejection cause — assert it in tests
  [ ] Non-square specs, and specs with different print vs digital sizes
  [ ] GPS EXIF must be stripped — privacy requirement, test it explicitly
